    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1077">

                <pb facs="0804" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1346</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Representative Rodgers to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-21T19:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 21, 1916, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>301. Department’s 307, August 19, noon. Cabrera to-day promised instruction to
                    State Governments to desist from action seeking to compel operation mines before
                    protection and transportation can be guaranteed. As to matter extension time
                    payment taxes last tercio without penalty promised consideration question.</p>
                <p>As to general question mining taxes status about same as stated in my 229, July
                    21, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rodgers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
